# Nissan Qashqai J11 five-door crossover, 2014-2021.
#
# The second-generation Qashqai. The pre-facelift car (2014-2017) is modelled:
# the facelift changed the bumpers, grille and lamps but not the shell, and the
# only flank photograph available is of a facelift car.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Qashqai
#
# Dimensions 4.380 x 1.800 x 1.590 m, wheelbase 2.646 m, from the English
# Wikipedia J11 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 2.050 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the J11 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, red, black and blue. Weights white 3, red 3, black 2,
# blue 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 185 km/h for the 1.2 DIG-T, the volume model. Comfort 95/473, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 95, a step above the J10's 125-minute figure on the older scale
# because the J11 rides better. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 2014 intro, retires staggered 2029-2032 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-qashqai-j11.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-qashqai-j11.dae (53 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-qashqai-j11/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitations: the flank photograph (image 1) is a 2017 facelift car
# used for the shell only, with the roof rack deliberately not modelled, and all
# four photographs are three-quarter views rather than level profiles. The nose
# is more angular than the car and the tail-lamp surfaces read slightly
# discontinuously. At 128 px the tall crossover body, the shoulder line and the
# V-grille read as the J11.

